WHAT WAS REMOVED, AND WHY
-------------------------
stmlib is mixed. One file in it, stmlib/ui/event_queue.h, carries a
GPL-3.0-or-later header rather than the MIT one — it belongs to the
firmware's front-panel code, not to the DSP. It was vendored by the initial
copy and has been deleted, along with the seven module ui.h headers that
were the only things including it (braids, clouds, elements, peaks, plaits,
rings, warps). None of them was ever reachable from a compiled translation
unit, so no GPL code was ever linked into the plugin — but it was being
redistributed in this source tree, which is its own obligation, and that is
now not the case. Nothing under this directory mentions the GPL any more.

TRADEMARK
---------
"Mutable Instruments" is a registered trademark, and the README asks that
neither it nor the original module names appear on derived work. No block in
Quadrat carries a Mutable name; each is named for what it does.
Correspondence of the code, for anyone reading it:

    macro    plaits        scatter  clouds
    reson    rings         mallet   elements
    xmod     warps         timbre   braids
    drum     peaks

Only the modules actually used are vendored. Marbles, Stages, Tides, Streams
and Frames are MIT too and can be added the same way; their firmware-shaped
APIs (gate-flag arrays, ramp extractors, configure-time topology) need more
than a parameter mapping, so they are not here yet.
